    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d105">

                <pb facs="0227" n="133" sameAs="frus:frus1896/pg133"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Rockhill to Mr. Patenôtre.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-07-25"><hi rendition="#italic">July 25,
                        1896</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 69.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the
                    receipt of your note of the 22d instant, stating that Madagascar has been
                    declared a French colony by a law which implies the abrogation of the treaties
                    signed by the Hova Government, and substitutes for those the conventions
                    existing between the United States and France.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. W. Rockhill</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
